[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2981780207","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107594#issuecomment-2981780207","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107594","id":2981780207,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6xulrv","user":{"login":"Bromeon","id":708488,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwODQ4OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/708488?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon","html_url":"https://github.com/Bromeon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-17T20:43:39Z","updated_at":"2025-06-17T20:43:39Z","body":"I think you mentioned it @dsnopek, but I don't remember: what was the reason again for `frame_func` to exist, in addition to `_process()`? \r\n\r\nAlso in light of the https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/12622 initiative, which wants to move  hardcoded .h functionality to the .json file :slightly_smiling_face: ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2981780207/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2981886006","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107594#issuecomment-2981886006","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107594","id":2981886006,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6xu_g2","user":{"login":"dsnopek","id":191561,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MTU2MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191561?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek","html_url":"https://github.com/dsnopek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-17T21:27:18Z","updated_at":"2025-06-17T21:27:59Z","body":"> I think you mentioned it @dsnopek, but I don't remember: what was the reason again for `frame_func` to exist, in addition to `_process()`?\r\n\r\nIt's to make a GDExtension equivalent to `ScriptLanguage::frame()` (that's why the comment makes reference to `ScriptServer::frame()` which is what calls that method on all the registered script languages). If your GDExtension is just binding a language, like the C# GDExtension binding, there is no `Node` to put a `_process()` method on.\r\n\r\nThere are some workarounds, but they are awkward.\r\n\r\nFor example, with the the `startup_func`, you can now access the main loop, and if it's `SceneTree`, you can connect to the `process_frame` signal. However, it's not uncommon to replace the main loop in automated tests, and you wouldn't want your language binding to stop working in that case. :-) There's also a workaround involving `RenderingServer`, but it's weird for a language binding to depend on `RenderingServer` when it has nothing to do with rendering.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2981886006/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2982812924","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107594#issuecomment-2982812924","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107594","id":2982812924,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6xyhz8","user":{"login":"Bromeon","id":708488,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwODQ4OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/708488?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon","html_url":"https://github.com/Bromeon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-18T06:08:04Z","updated_at":"2025-06-18T06:08:04Z","body":"Thank you very much! :+1: \r\nDo you think it makes sense to add a short version of this to the `frame_func` docs as well? ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2982812924/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2984077504","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107594#issuecomment-2984077504","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107594","id":2984077504,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6x3WjA","user":{"login":"dsnopek","id":191561,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MTU2MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191561?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek","html_url":"https://github.com/dsnopek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-18T12:52:34Z","updated_at":"2025-06-18T12:52:34Z","body":"> Do you think it makes sense to add a short version of this to the `frame_func` docs as well?\r\n\r\nSure, I added this additional comment:\r\n\r\n```\r\n// This is intended to be the equivalent of `ScriptLanguage::frame()` for GDExtension language bindings that don't use the script API.\r\n```\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2984077504/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,